{"version":3,"title":"30-day beginner DSA plan","start_date":"2026-10-18","end_date":"2026-11-16","placement_day":"2026-12-01","post_plan":{"start":"2026-11-17","end":"2026-12-03","focus":["CS core intensive (OOP 2d, DBMS 4d, OS 4d, CN 3d)","daily mock OA","stretch: hard problems on patterns already learned","verbal explanation practice","Full stack upskilling (HTTP/REST, rendering & state, auth, ORM, web security) in Java"]},"problem_count":120,"skim_count":8,"clusters":[{"key":"arrays-hashing","title":"Arrays & hashing","days":[1,2,3,4,5]},{"key":"search-strings","title":"Search, strings & sorting","days":[6,7,8,9]},{"key":"linear-ds","title":"Linked lists & stacks","days":[10,11,12,13]},{"key":"recursion-greedy-heaps","title":"Recursion, backtracking, greedy & heaps","days":[14,15,16,17]},{"key":"trees","title":"Trees","days":[18,19,20,21]},{"key":"graphs","title":"Graphs","days":[22,23,24]},{"key":"dp","title":"Dynamic programming & tries/bits","days":[25,26,27,28,29,30]}],"roles":{"LEARN":{"meaning":"First contact with a pattern. Read the full Note-this pipeline (and the linked theory) BEFORE coding, then close it and code from an empty file.","weight":10},"APPLY":{"meaning":"Same pattern, new wording. Attempt cold with the stuck ladder. Pipeline stays covered until you have tried.","weight":10},"TWIST":{"meaning":"The pattern plus one modification. Attempt cold; the brainstorm stage names the modification once you reveal it.","weight":10},"DISGUISE":{"meaning":"The pattern hidden inside a story. Clearing it is the proof that the pattern transfers.","weight":10}},"daily_blocks":[{"key":"resolves","title":"Due re-solves","minutes":20,"note":"cold re-solve of problems due at +2/+7/+14 days, oldest first; max 2 per day"},{"key":"must_sibling","title":"Yesterday's must-study siblings","minutes":30,"note":"one per problem solved yesterday; read the mini-pipeline, write the pseudocode on paper"},{"key":"micro","title":"Micro-theory and pattern card","minutes":10},{"key":"problems","title":"Today's 4 problems","minutes":150,"note":"paper: analyse -> brainstorm -> algorithm -> pseudocode; then code; then Note-this card"},{"key":"drill","title":"Recognition drill","minutes":10,"note":"5 unseen statements: name the pattern and one-line approach, no code"},{"key":"cs_core","title":"CS core card","minutes":20}],"floor":["resolves","the day's first LEARN problem"],"never_miss_twice":"a missed day is allowed; on the next day the floor is mandatory before anything else","cut_order":[{"step":1,"action":"drop optional siblings (they stay browsable, never scheduled)"},{"step":2,"action":"DISGUISE problem moves to the revision queue with a due date 7 days out"},{"step":3,"action":"TWIST problem is downgraded to SKIM: reveal the pipeline, write the pseudocode on paper, do not code"}],"carry_over":"unfinished LEARN and APPLY problems from past days appear in a capped 'carried over' list (max 4) above today's problems; days never move and the plan is never redrawn","calibration":{"day":7,"rule":"if the measured median pace over days 1-7 is below 4 problems/day, cut-order step 2 applies permanently to days 8-30. This is the only allowed recalibration."},"change_budget":"design changes only in the Sunday 20-minute review, at most one per week","stuck_ladder":[{"from_min":0,"to_min":10,"do":"Fill the analysis box on paper and write the dumbest correct (brute force) solution. Most 'stuck' is a skipped brute force."},{"from_min":10,"to_min":20,"do":"Read the constraints and turn n into a target complexity. Point at the line of your brute force that does the most repeated work and name WHY it is wasted."},{"from_min":20,"to_min":30,"do":"Read the theory section linked on this rung. Reveal only the Analyse stage. Close it and try again."},{"from_min":30,"to_min":40,"do":"Reveal the Brainstorm stage (brute -> optimal). Close it, write the algorithm in words and the pseudocode yourself, then code."},{"from_min":40,"to_min":999,"do":"Reveal everything (or watch the linked video). Then close every tab and code it from an empty file. Mark it revisit with confidence <= 3 - it comes back as a re-solve."}],"ai_protocol":["Never before the 20 minute mark. The struggle is what encodes it.","Never paste the problem and ask for a solution.","Ask: 'Here is my approach: X. Where does it break?'","Ask: 'What invariant should I be maintaining here?'","Ask: 'I have an O(n^2). What property of the input am I not exploiting?'","After solving: 'Here is my code, review it like a FAANG interviewer.' Most valuable, least used.","Separate session, always. Keeps you from asking earlier and earlier.","Anything that needed a hint is not done, it is scheduled. Set confidence <= 3 and redo it cold in 48 hrs."],"tag_seed":["stuck","off-by-one","wrong-complexity","misread-constraints","slow-implementation","ask-in-mock","elegant","redo-cold","template-drilled","interview-asked","no-pseudocode","recognised-in-drill"],"statuses":["todo","solved","revisit","skimmed"],"days":[{"day":1,"date":"2026-10-18","weekday":"Sun","cluster":"arrays-hashing","title":"Array traversal and in-place writes","content":"ready","problems":["running-sum-of-1d-array","max-consecutive-ones","move-zeroes","remove-duplicates-from-sorted-array"],"skims":[],"micro":{"title":"Day 1 — one pass, a few variables, and writing in place","theory":["arr-single-pass-running-state","arr-read-write-pointer","cx-big-o","cpp-vector","meta-analyse-a-problem"]},"reading_path":[{"page":"meta-analyse-a-problem","section":"five-questions","minutes":4},{"page":"meta-bottleneck-method","section":"idea","minutes":3},{"page":"meta-pseudocode-format","section":"five-slots","minutes":3},{"page":"cx-big-o","section":"counting","minutes":3},{"page":"cpp-vector","section":"basics","minutes":2},{"page":"arr-single-pass-running-state","section":"idea","minutes":3},{"page":"arr-read-write-pointer","section":"idea","minutes":3}],"core":{"subject":"OOP","title":"Classes, objects and their memory · Cons